The tree was committed unmodified first (git history: "vendor: OpenRSP 3.15.2-20 source, unmodified"),
so `git diff <that commit> -- vendor/openrsp` shows every change below exactly.

Changes made for VibeSDR (GPLv3 section 5a notice). Each is marked "VibeSDR change (2026-10-21)" in the
file, and each leaves upstream behaviour unchanged unless the option is set:

1. cmake/Platform.cmake — SDRPLAY_LINUX_UDEV (default ON). OFF builds the Linux service without
   libudev. Only the hotplug monitor uses libudev and nothing in the service calls it.
2. cmake/Platform.cmake — SDRPLAY_LIBUSB_LIBRARY / SDRPLAY_LIBUSB_INCLUDE_DIR name libusb explicitly
   instead of asking pkg-config (VibeServer links its own static libusb 1.0.30, built without udev).
3. CMakeLists.txt — SDRPLAY_STATIC_CXX_RUNTIME (default OFF). ON links libstdc++/libgcc statically
   into libsdrplay_api.so.3.15 and sdrplay_apiService, so the package depends on nothing but glibc.

How VibeServer builds it: vibeserver/CMakeLists.txt, section "OpenRSP". docs/OPENRSP-BUNDLE-PLAN.md
gives the reasoning, and covers each platform.
